From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Williams <alexis@typedr.at>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:34:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] schema: let a front end set the page size

A schema reads its page size from menu/page_size when it is loaded, and
the menu, the selector and the API all read it from the schema. A front
end that keeps the page size as a setting of its own sets it on each
session's schema, so a change reaches running sessions at once, without
compiling every schema's config again to change one number.
---
 src/rime/schema.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/rime/schema.h b/src/rime/schema.h
index bb68bcd..76578a5 100644
--- a/src/rime/schema.h
+++ b/src/rime/schema.h
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ class Schema {
   void set_config(Config* config) { config_.reset(config); }
 
   int page_size() const { return page_size_; }
+  void set_page_size(int page_size) { page_size_ = page_size; }
   bool page_down_cycle() const { return page_down_cycle_; }
   const string& select_keys() const { return select_keys_; }
   void set_select_keys(const string& keys) { select_keys_ = keys; }
